    "type": "question",
    "label": "73",
    "prompt": "Solve the following equation.\n$$(x+1)(x+2)(x-5)(x-6)=98$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=2\\pm\\sqrt2,\\ 2\\pm\\sqrt{23}$.\n\nPair the factors and substitute $u=(x-2)^2$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x+1)(x-5)&=(x-2)^2-9\\\\(x+2)(x-6)&=(x-2)^2-16.\\end{align*}$$\nLet $u=(x-2)^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(u-9)(u-16)&=98\\\\u^2-25u+144&=98\\\\u^2-25u+46&=0\\\\(u-2)(u-23)&=0\\\\u&=2\\text{ or }23.\\end{align*}$$\nHence $(x-2)^2=2$ or $23$, giving\n$$x=2\\pm\\sqrt2,\\quad2\\pm\\sqrt{23}.$$\nFor $u=2$, the original product is $(-7)(-14)=98$; for $u=23$, it is $14\\times7=98$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
